The use of ".e" for "je" was a typo, and changing it constitutes
the first part of Official Typo Correction #4.  There are two
occurrences of this sentence: in the CEhE section and in the
PEhE section.

> secondly, I thought this sentence means:
> 
>   I am a friend of you, and John is a friend of James.

No, it means {I}                {John}
                 are-a-friend-of
             {you}              {James}
 
